    "field": "Climate change impact on snow water resources",
    "problem": "Accurately attributing and projecting near-term snowpack loss in the western United States is challenging because the combined influences of anthropogenic forcing and internal decadal variability remain poorly quantified.",
    "method": "This study uses large ensembles of global climate model simulations with different forcings, combined with observations and an optimal fingerprinting analysis, to attribute the causes of recent snowpack loss and project its substantial near-term decline over the western United States.",
    "task": "The task is to use a large ensemble of climate simulations to quantify the contributions of anthropogenic forcing and internal variability to observed and projected near-term snowpack loss over the western United States.",
